# b. Using the same name but nChar is 20, it will print all characters but will encounter an error message "IndexError: string index out of range".
# c. To fix the error, we can add a condition statement to check whether the inputed nChar is greater than the number of characters in the name. If it is, we can set the nChar into the length of the name to avoid the index error.

# Code 1 : Modified
def greet_students(name, nChar):
    if nChar > len(name):
        nChar = len(name)
    for i in range(nChar):
        print(name[i])

name = input("Enter a Name : ")
nChar = input("Enter any numeric number : ")
nChar = int(nChar)
greet_students(name, nChar)

